  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/clibanarius_africanus_en/",
      "html": "<p>The charming hermit crab Clibanarius africanus has become a very popular aquarium inhabitant. It is a euryhaline species, which means that it can survive in both pure fresh and pure marine water. However, it seems that it can live in pure freshwater only for a few months, so it is much better to keep it in brackish water.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/clibanarius_africanus_en/",
      "html": "<p>Clibanarius are detritus feeders. Detritus is composed of various dead plant and animal matter. In the aquarium, Clibanarius feed readily on any typical fish food.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "notes",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/31-crayfishes-shrimps-crabs-snails-mussels/clibanarius_africanus_en/",
      "html": "<p>C. africanus are usually imported with the brown shells of the snail species Tympanotonus fuscatus, but occasionally they bear the white shells of the snail Pachymelania aurita.</p><p>Lexicon: Clibanarius: term for a heavily armoured cavalryman. africanus: means \"comes from Africa\".</p>"
    }
  ],
